    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d861">

                <pb facs="0993" n="897" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg897"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">667.003/124: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner at Constantinople</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-06-21T18:00:00+03:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 21, 1921—6
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 22—9:22
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>203. My telegram number 190, June 7, 5 p.m. Turkish Government informally
                    indicates willingness to revert to pre-war system of taxation in case the powers
                    will consent to a temporary increase in ad valorem rate to 14 or 15 percent to
                    meet urgent needs of Treasury, (see Department’s telegram 86 of November
                        15th<anchor n="10" xml:id="d861-f1"/>), this increase to be enforced until
                    final determination of tariff system under peace treaty.</p>
                <p>I consider this most opportune moment for bringing pressure to bear in London,
                    Paris and Rome. Request information of action taken.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bristol</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
